entials","k":"bank","la":62.022677,"lo":-6.765373,"d":1854,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-16:00","f":["wc"]},{"n":"Bónus","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":62.005383,"lo":-6.801705,"d":1916,"h":"Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00","w":"Bonus.fo","ad":"10 Janusargøta","f":["wc"]},{"n":"St. Mary's Church, Tórshavn","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.014472,"lo":-6.779778,"d":1217,"ds":"The St. Mary's Church (Faroese: Mariukirkjan) is a parish of the Roman Catholic Church located in Mariugøta 4 in the city of Tórshavn, the capital of the Faroe Islands, in the Diocese of Copenhagen. While Catholicism was present in the Faroes from 999 AD, after the Danish Reformation, the last Catholic bishop in the islands was executed in 1538.","wpu":"St. Mary's Church, Tórshavn","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Maria-Kirken2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Nólsoy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.009167,"lo":-6.668611,"d":5042,"ds":"Nólsoy (Faroese pronunciation: [ˈnœlsɪ], previously also Nölsoy; Danish: Nolsø; Old Norse: Norsey) is an island and village in central Faroe Islands, 4km east of the capital Tórshavn in Streymoy.","wpu":"Nólsoy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/N%C3%B3lsoy_by_Maciej_Brencz_%281%29.jpg/960px-N%C3%B3lsoy_by_Maciej_Brencz_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Velbastaður","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.984722,"lo":-6.850556,"d":5054,"ds":"Velbastaður (Danish: Velbestad) is a village on the island of Streymoy in the Faroe Islands. It is a part of Tórshavn Municipality and is considered among the oldest settlements in the islands. There are two schools and one kindergarten in the village, with children coming from the neighboring village of Kirkjubø as well as the capital at Tórshavn.","wpu":"Velbastaður","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Velbasta%C3%B0ur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG/960px-Velbasta%C3%B0ur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gamlarætt","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.9625,"lo":-6.818611,"d":5589,"ds":"Gamlarætt is a ferry port in the Faroe Islands. It is situated on the southwestern side of the island of Streymoy, the largest island in the Faroes, between the villages of Velbastaður and Kirkjubøur. It accommodates ferry services to the islands of Sandoy and Hestur.","wpu":"Gamlarætt","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Luftfoto_af_Gamlar%C3%A6tt.jpg/960px-Luftfoto_af_Gamlar%C3%A6tt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Syðradalur, Streymoy Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.024167,"lo":-6.91,"d":7830,"ds":"Syðradalur (Danish: Sydredal) is a small village in the Faroe Islands. It is located on the west coast of Streymoy, in Tórshavn Municipality. Not to be confused with Syðradalur village on Kalsoy, it has a view at the islands Koltur and Vágar.","wpu":"Syðradalur, Streymoy Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sy%C3%B0radalur%2C_Streymoy%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG/960px-Sy%C3%B0radalur%2C_Streymoy%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Æðuvík","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.069722,"lo":-6.69,"d":8092,"ds":"Æðuvík (/ˈɛaʋʊˌʋʊik/ from Æða meaning \"duck\" and vík meaning \"bay\", Danish: Avevig) is a community located on the southernmost tip of Eysturoy island of the Faroe Islands. Founded in 1897, its postal code is FO 645. Its population is about 100, and it is located at N 62° 4' 11 W 6° 41' 24.","wpu":"Æðuvík","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/%C3%86%C3%B0uv%C3%ADk_seen_from_helicopter.jpg/960px-%C3%86%C3%B0uv%C3%ADk_seen_from_helicopter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nes, Eysturoy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.079722,"lo":-6.707778,"d":8723,"ds":"Nes (Danish: Næs) is a village in Nes Municipality on the southwest coast of the Faroese island of Eysturoy.","wpu":"Nes, Eysturoy","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Nes%2C_Faroe_Islands_%284%29.JPG/960px-Nes%2C_Faroe_Islands_%284%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hestur","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.952778,"lo":-6.894444,"d":8985,"ds":"Hestur (Danish: Hestø) is an island in the central Faroe Islands, to the west of Streymoy and the south of Koltur. Hestur means horse in Faroese. On the west coast is a guillemot colony.","wpu":"Hestur","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Hestur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG/960px-Hestur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Norðradalur","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.040278,"lo":-6.922778,"d":9069,"ds":"Norðradalur (Danish: Nordredal) is a village on the western coast of the Faroese island of Streymoy in Tórshavn Municipality. The 2015 population was 15. Its postal code is FO 178.","wpu":"Norðradalur","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Nor%C3%B0radalur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG/960px-Nor%C3%B0radalur%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sornfelli","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.083333,"lo":-6.833333,"d":9307,"ds":"Sornfelli is a mountain plateau on the island of Streymoy in the Faroe Islands about 12 km from the capital Tórshavn (20 km by road), in the Mjørkadalur valley. It is the site of a NATO military radar station at 725m above sea level (asl). The Sornfelli Meteorological Station installed in 1999 is located in the middle of the 40,000 m2 Sornfelli Mountain top plateau, also at 725m above sea level.","wpu":"Sornfelli","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Mountain_Sornfelli.1.JPG/960px-Mountain_Sornfelli.1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Toftir","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.088889,"lo":-6.735556,"d":9343,"ds":"Toftir (Danish: Tofte) Faroese: [ˈtʰɔftəɹ] is a village in Nes Municipality on the island of Eysturoy, in the Faroe Islands. It is part of a chain of villages stretching over a distance of 10 kilometers on the east side of Skálafjørður (fjord) on Eysturoy island.","wpu":"Toftir","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Toftir%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG/960px-Toftir%2C_Faroe_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Tórshavn (Faroese: [ˈtʰɔu̯ʂhau̯n] ; lit. 'Thor's harbour'; Danish: Thorshavn), locally referred to as Havn, is the capital and largest city of the Faroe Islands. It is located in the southern part on the east coast of Streymoy. To the northwest of the city lies the 347-meter-high (1,138 ft) mountain Húsareyn, and to the southwest, the 350-meter-high (1,150 ft) Kirkjubøreyn.","wpu":"Tórshavn","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Is03002-Torshavn.jpg/960px-Is03002-Torshavn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}